      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1900-07-13_WidnesExaminer_art0015" n="art0015">
        <head>PARR'S BANK LIMITED.</head>
        <p>PARR'S BANK LIMITED.</p>
        <p>Increase of Capital. Purchase of Dumbell's Bank.</p>
        <p>An eatraoriiinary general meeting of Parr's Bank Limited, was held in London on Monday, for the pun pnv,, et' wysirag resolutions for the increase f ranital to .17,317,5C0 by the er,atinn of 4,675 shares of £lOO each. The directors of the bank haying arranged for the put- chase of the Ashton,Stalybridge,Hyde and Glossop Bank, 1.250°f the shares thus cre4ted are to be allotted to the shareholders of that bank, in accT,rdanea with an agree- ment made with that bank and its liquidators, the shares So allocated to iyartieipite in the cristrihutiA.in of profits from and after the 31‘t D ,cemb,r, 1900. The remainder of the 4,675 shares are to be offered to the members of the company whose names appear on the regie,r of the crlnnanT on 18 h July, 1900, at the price of £7O per share of which £2O are to be paid as capita and £5O as premium, pay.ble at such date or dates as the direc'ors preecribri. Mr. C F PARR. the chairman of the bark, in moving the adoption of the resolutions, explained the necessity for increasing the capital, sing that the Ash- ton and Stalybridye Bank had been carrying on a small but sound husine4s, ani it had he,n going on a long time. The net market price was £9O over the par value so that in elfrrring shares the present holders at a prenp'um of £7O it c:orild be equivalent to a bones of £2O to each sharel-eilcler, which was a 'very handsome b ,nus indeed The new shares we'd he issued in tae propor- tion of one ',harp to every £2O shar-• already held. The creation of 3.425 pew .harr, he npotted to the present shareholders would add £6B 500 to the paid up capital of the hank The nremium of £5O per share on these would produce £171.250. Of this anv,nnt it was pr mosed to carry £6B 521 to the reserve fund. They wcuid have peen in he papera that tire dir ctors of thi-i bank had bought the go:017M of Dumbell's Bank, in the Is e of Man, for £40.000, and they ProPos, d that that Fu.n Ph, OA he paid out of this prEna;urn. an I the bilanee of £62,271 they proposed to transfer to the pr • petty account.</p>
        <p>Mr. Nix srelnil.rl the vs,thitions, which werp eatried unanimously. 'The Ci,airman th,. confirma- tion woulii Nitre p'ac. at the geurni mecting at Miring - ton in a fortr,ight'i time</p>
