        <p>- - The c0mn.i.,,0 d•cid. d to v'j mirn the appeal: 'ME AcSESSMF.NT OF MESSRS. GREENALL'S BREWERY. OwEN se ~t,-.4 ar. p rc-as,•einrmit of 211eSsrs. or-en 11. Whitler •nd G mpany's hr.wery at Wiiderspo I. Re p1:c..3 the assessmsnt of the tc•tlinx stores at £2BB ,r• s- and £237 10. rateable. The brewery itself. ~• .to ..• •ei • and w‘shlng shed. ile valued at £1,837 grof 8 and £1,491 rate ble.He pointed out in‘t tekl 6 d,..1 noth,,,g I r V -lue *lion miebt be said to evst neCAUI th" firm ownf-d ,ied h .12S3S.The difficulty was to adopt shit he inieh• term a tient' • mental value and make it real valu". If the committee Dut up tt e gross to thehir amount which had been soggested they w•ire inchilog profits which were not in lic propfry but something m•ds in con-equeme of it. Ins question fcr the c! comi'tee to decide was whether Ut addition to the viluei h. (Mr. Omen) hal put on the brewery s,mathieg ought to be added for the value 'which was nor there, hut which was sad to fxl:t He Was prepared to subitAntiate his valuation in any court of law. The CLEnic .fave it as his opinion that the committea 'were entitled to take in'o consideration the number of tied houses belonging to the firm as an element to be oonsldered in the valnation of the a,sissment. There vas not, however, any clearly established decision en ttte matter. The committee coincided with the views of the Clerk but &amp;Wed to reittice their orieinal assessment of 22,200 gross to £2OOO gross and £l.BOO rsteable, which is a slight increase upon Mr Oven's vslaation in con- Sideration of the tied h-us..s owned by thr firm. Mr. H. Harrom ( \feasts. Robert D ivieS and Co.). appeared on behalf of Metzsrs Gr,ensll, whitlev and and was informed of the deciainn ef the committee. /le then raked whet er in the event of the directors appealirre ti Quirter Se,sioss, the committee Would consent to mei, valuer (Mr. Owen) and the 'valuer of the lirewrr- (;,nineny haying a meeting to eonfer on points of differe