        <p>At Liverpo don z'..aturday Dacia Duncan Lamb, aged 24,waN charged on remand with having forged cheques at Mancnester and Warrington for over £2,000 while manager of a suburban branch of the Bank of Liverpool. It will be remembered that the prisoner ab.conded with the money, and was arrestel while on a fishing excursion at Duns, Berwickshire, where he was living in con.Verable style. The prisoner tow pleaded guilty to stealing £l5O, and the charge of forgery was withdrawn. Counsel for the prosecution stated that the bunk had recovered something like 90 per cent of tne money, and tney were content to leave the matter in the magistrates' hands without further investi- gation.—Un behalf of the prisoner it was urged that be had marrie.l on an insuffietent income, and get- ting into difficulties had committed the crime on the impuke of the moment If lie were treated as a fist offender his friends would send him abroad and give him a now start.—The Stipendiary Magis- trate adopted this course, an the prisoner Was bound over tinier the Faro'. Off •nrisAl, Act.</p>
