        <p>Lots 1 and 2 are held with other property on an underlease dated atcl July, 1878, for a term of 915 years from 25th March 1878. at an anima ground rent of £1 48 61 and are sold for the residue excep% the last three d tys of the said term and subject to the lessees covenants contained in the said underlease and as to Lot 1 to an annual ground rent of 25 and as to Lot 2 to an annual ground rent of £5 4s 6d. Lai' 3.—THEWS. LBI4.3IMOLD DWALLOI.I--11OUiRS. Nos. 32, 64, and 66 Hoyle-street, Bew ey-rossl, Warrington and a plot of building Land adjoining same. This Lot con- tains an araa of 915 superficial squsre yar is or the:etbouts anti will be sold or the to idue cmcopt the la t three days of a term of 999 years from the let Has, 1875 subject to an annual ground rent of £ll 89 9d and to the covemtnts con- tained in an indenture of underlease da'e 1 the 2:lth June 1878 under which the said prinnises are held _ .</p>
