        <p>LOT S.—EIGHT corrAlES NO3 22 to 38 (even numbers) inclusive in Watkin-street. Warrington. This Lot is he d with other twooe-ty hereafter mentioned for a term of 98J years created by Unierlease dated the 23rd day of August 1883 at a ground rent of £22 per annum. The remainier of the property comprised in this Unclerle-.se has been leased for a term of 950 years rorn 25th Manta 1893 at an annual ground rent of £l4 17s 9d and the whole of the property will be sold for the residue of the said term of 93) years at the said ground rent of £22 per annum subject to the said sub!ease but with the ben fit of the said groan t rent of £1; t7s 9cl thereby reserve i and or the coven ants by the sublessee therein contained. Quass rental £32 9s 91 per allfluln. Lo r6.—TWO DWRLLING-HOUSE3 NO3. 23 and 30, Lovely-lane. Warrintton. Rent £39 per annum. The property is held with other propert7 under an Under- Tease dated 31st December 1377 and wilt be sold for the resi- due of a term of 998 years frarn the 10th A.agnst .877 except the last 10 days ther,of subject to the p tyrn -int of the yearly rent of £5 (part of an annua rent of 23:6, 9d) and to the covenants and conditions contained in said timid .r;ease. For further particulars apply as to lots 4 and sto Messrs John White Mac Iver an Gampany, Land Ageats and inr- veyors. 23, Bold-street, Virar.ingi an, and as t,) all the said lots to the Augloneer, Bewsay Chambers. W., rriugkin, or ta Mff3SRS. WO.)Di AND SON. Solicitors. Wallington.</p>
