        <p>SHOP-BREAKERS WELL PUNISRED.—Thomas Duffey and James Green were charged on remand with b ing found on the inclosed premises of +desire. Pov .y and Duckworth, pro vision dealers, 20 and 22. Buttermuket street, at 9.3 i p in on July 3rd, for an nnlawfal purl:me namely with intent to commit a felony.—From Superintendent Monagla in's state- ment of the facts of the case it appeare I that at 8.33 on the night in question the shop was locked up. A man named Pennington and assistants were working in the back premises at about 9.3 I when they heard a noise At the back door whish led to the shop One of the assistants went to see what was the matter, and be found the prisoner Duff ay inside the shop. The dear had be n broken open. Green WAS in the entry and bath prisoners ran ott but were eventu- ally arrested by P.C. Monks. Prisoners were brought up I tst week and remanded in order that inquiries might be made It appeared that Duffey had been onvicted 16 times for different offences including .hp braeking Green hid been convicted nine times. —Prisoners were seat to gaol for three months with hard labour.</p>
