l. PIITS'd have opportunely helped innumerable oung couples " over the stile," and lived to assist their P cltdren in like manner. PITTS'S at the present time have 1;14,00 out, and over 800 customers paying instalments. -PITTS'S ENDEAVOUR ALWAYS TO OBLIGE JL CUSTOMERS, and this is appreciated, as the following entirely unsolicited letter, one of thousands received, shows " Hyde. April 18th. 1900.—Dear sirs,-1t is wit GREAT SATISFACTIO that I send you a kind word of acknow- -I,ogment. thanking you not heartily, for the HONEST. STRA IGHTFORWARD. and LIBERAL wry with which I have been dealt with. Wishing you and your business every success.—Yours truly," T. 0." Name withheld for obvious reasons, but PITTS'S can produce the original if need be. F'S ARE VIEWED WITH FAVOUR BY THE PRESS, having received, unasked for eulogistic notices from the following . " Peudieton Reporter" "Criterion," "Lancashire Review," "Salford Chronicle," " Bo.ton News and Journal." Leigt, Chronicle."" Warring- ton Observer," "Warrington Examber," " Oldham Stan- dard," " Shottin's Advertiser," " South Manchester Chronic'e." " Western Telegraph." 'Gentleman's Journal," " Manclsester Faces and Plaees." AC., As. • PITTS'S IS NOT A LIMITED COMPANY,but a private concern, owned by Samuel Pitts alone, there foie PITTS'a can accept as LITTLE PROFIT as they think fit without having first to consult a host of shareholders clamouring for large ividends, which, ot course, necessitates heavy profits. PI CTs'S own resources are amply sufficient for the economical working of PITTs'S enormous business. PITT'S FAR-FAMED HOUSES OF FORM- TURE, at 15f, 221, 28i, 381, 50, 75, 100, 200, up to LOGO guineas are renowed for superlative excellence and thorough durability. 'They challenge the most critical judgment. Their MAUVELLOUS Y.aiAlic is simply astounling. It is the bounaen duty of everyone to see them before deciding, as connoisseurs consider each is honestly worth DOUBLiii the rice asked. Full parti.sulars at request. PITTS'zi ILLUSTRATED FURNISHING GUIDE is universally recognised es the handsomest and most comprehensive extant. it contains 70,0 extremely artistic designs, priced, and shows plainly HOW TO SAVE, 01411- HALF. Each costs us one shilling. We send it pst free, gratis. DIT rs's CARPETS and FLOOR COVERING-i.— Grand Display. All British makes, choicest designs. many of which exclusive; exquisitely blended colourings. Laid and fitted free of charge by competent men. PITTS'S BEDSTEADS. PIANOS CYCLES, Bassinet tea, Mail Carts, Lamps, Mina. Glass. Earthe- nware. Magnificent selection. Astonishing value. SAMUEL PITTS. MANCHESTER. i LONDON-ROAD (Ardwiek, and Longsight, cars). GAYTHO tiN (all City-road cars pass Door.) EstaMished 1845. National Telephone 1124.</p>
